# Maintain ENHANCEMENTS.md

Whenever this work adds or materially changes **user-visible behavior**, update **[ENHANCEMENTS.md](../../ENHANCEMENTS.md)** in the **same change** (same PR / same chat session).

## Must update

- New UI flows (popup, options page, buttons, panels).
- New or removed AI providers, auth flows, or storage keys affecting setup.
- Manifest changes (`permissions`, `host_permissions`, new pages).
- Breaking changes to configuration or defaults.

## Skip for pure internals

Refactors, renames, tests-only changes, or comment-only edits that do **not** affect shipped UX may omit a changelog line unless they unblock a user-visible fix worth mentioning.

## How to write entries

1. **Order (reverse chronological)**: Under **`## Changelog`**, put **`### Unreleased`** first when it has bullets. Below that, version sections **`### X.Y.Z — YYYY-MM-DD`** run **newest first** (matching [`manifest.json`](../../src/static/manifest/manifest.json) recency). Historical baselines (e.g. **1.0.1 — baseline**) stay **last**.
2. Prefer **`### Unreleased`** bullets during iteration; move under **`### X.Y.Z — YYYY-MM-DD`** when versioning matches `manifest.json`.
3. Be concise: **what** changed and **who cares** (one line each).
4. Link optional paths only when they help readers (`src/…`), not every file touched.

Before finishing the task, confirm **ENHANCEMENTS.md** reflects what an end user would notice.

## Popup changelog

User-facing bullets also appear in **[`src/shared/popupChangelog.ts`](../../src/shared/popupChangelog.ts)** (plain text for the toolbar popup). When you add or change **Unreleased** / version sections in **ENHANCEMENTS.md**, update **`POPUP_CHANGELOG`** in the same change so the popup stays accurate.

### Always include Unreleased items

**Unreleased** bullets in `ENHANCEMENTS.md` **must** have a matching section in `POPUP_CHANGELOG` with `title: "Unreleased"` at the top of the array. This lets the developer confirm which build they are testing by checking the **Info** tab in the extension popup.

- Add the `"Unreleased"` section as soon as the first unreleased bullet is written.
- Each bullet should be concise plain text (no markdown links).
- When cutting a release, rename the `"Unreleased"` title to the version string (e.g. `"1.0.6"`) and create a fresh empty `"Unreleased"` section **only if** new unreleased work continues in the same session.
